{"authored" [{"question" "q-81707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=-6{e}^{-2t}$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, find the velocity (in $\\text{m/s}$)  of the particle at time $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/state.json" "file_sha256" "2296cbc1e685f71bbd7568d3befc8cc6a391d1ac9241b66a01b7e6206a68a82c" "basis" 1299 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-6{e}^{-2t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-6(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2t})+C \\\\  & =3{e}^{-2t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3{e}^{0}+C \\\\ 2 & =3+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3{e}^{-2t}-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/state.json" "file_sha256" "2296cbc1e685f71bbd7568d3befc8cc6a391d1ac9241b66a01b7e6206a68a82c" "basis" 1299 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e452a65bf417c688343b895eee85ac72710dc818771994906dcc8abb1024b16" "basis" 1299 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/state.json" "file_sha256" "2296cbc1e685f71bbd7568d3befc8cc6a391d1ac9241b66a01b7e6206a68a82c" "basis" 1299 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(t)=-2{e}^{-2t}+4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/state.json" "file_sha256" "2296cbc1e685f71bbd7568d3befc8cc6a391d1ac9241b66a01b7e6206a68a82c" "basis" 1299 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(t)=-2{e}^{-t}+2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/state.json" "file_sha256" "2296cbc1e685f71bbd7568d3befc8cc6a391d1ac9241b66a01b7e6206a68a82c" "basis" 1299 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(t)=12{e}^{-t}-10"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/state.json" "file_sha256" "2296cbc1e685f71bbd7568d3befc8cc6a391d1ac9241b66a01b7e6206a68a82c" "basis" 1299 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(t)=3{e}^{-2t}+2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/state.json" "file_sha256" "2296cbc1e685f71bbd7568d3befc8cc6a391d1ac9241b66a01b7e6206a68a82c" "basis" 1299 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(t)=3{e}^{-2t}-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/state.json" "file_sha256" "2296cbc1e685f71bbd7568d3befc8cc6a391d1ac9241b66a01b7e6206a68a82c" "basis" 1299 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038230/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-7112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=2t-9{t}^{2}$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/state.json" "file_sha256" "516cb7280ecb25a1526f2933d869a59450e4b644d80f8245657f61fd273374d9" "basis" 2108 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-7112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (2t-9{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-3{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=-2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =(1)^{2}-3(1)^{3}+C \\\\ -2 & =1-3+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)={t}^{2}-3{t}^{3}.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =(2)^{2}-3(2)^{3} \\\\  & =4-24 \\\\  & =-20\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $20\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/state.json" "file_sha256" "516cb7280ecb25a1526f2933d869a59450e4b644d80f8245657f61fd273374d9" "basis" 2108 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-7112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b2f8408a328e5b806c1e628bc71ca6c654340d1174eadb0a141f5e98abbefdb" "basis" 2108 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-7112" "field"