s}$)  of the particle at time $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-6{e}^{-2t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-6(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2t})+C \\\\  & =3{e}^{-2t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3{e}^{0}+C \\\\ 2 & =3+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3{e}^{-2t}-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b7b5b06c7ea02565cd7e56c4cbd952b770b425f67eaedde2ecd298ea3061ce3"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "v(t)=-2{e}^{-2t}+4"] ["math" "v(t)=-2{e}^{-t}+2"] ["math" "v(t)=12{e}^{-t}-10"] ["math" "v(t)=3{e}^{-2t}+2"] ["math" "v(t)=3{e}^{-2t}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-81707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(t)=3{e}^{-2t}-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{ft}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=12{t}^{3}+20t,$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{ft/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=25\\,\\text{ft/s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (12{t}^{3}+20t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{4}+10{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=25.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25 & =3({1}^{4})+10({1}^{2})+C \\\\ 25 & =13+C \\\\ C & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3{t}^{4}+10{t}^{2}+12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b7b5b06c7ea02565cd7e56c4cbd952b770b425f67eaedde2ecd298ea3061ce3"} {"question" "q-351003" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351003" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3t^4+10t^2+12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in ${\\text{m /s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t),$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=10\\,\\text{m /s}$ when $t=\\pi \\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(\\pi )=10.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+C \\\\ 10 & =-6(-1)+C \\\\ 10 & =6+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b7b5b06c7ea02565cd7e56c4cbd952b770b425f67eaedde2ecd298ea3061ce3"} {"question" "q-351027" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351027" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6\\cos(t)+4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in ${\\text{ft/s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=\\frac{6}{{t}^{2}}-3,$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{ft/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=1\\,\\text{ft/s}$ when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{6}{{t}^{2}}-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{6}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+\\int (-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{t}-3t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(2)=1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{6}{2}-3(2)+C \\\\ 1 & =-9+C \\\\ C & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=-\\frac{6}{t}-3t+10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b7b5b06c7ea02565cd7e56c4cbd952b770b425f67eaedde2ecd298ea3061ce3"} {"question" "q-351051" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17c1de78e45024b07bcd436d7bc5f17d86"} {"question" "q-351051" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{6}{t}-3t+10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067094/state.json" "file_sha256" "9172eb7c2799bc8df135f6959862da17